    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.is_independent_set - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.is_independent_set.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.is_independent_set()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if a set of nodes forms an independent set.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.is_independent_set()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if a set of nodes forms an independent set.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.is_independent_set()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Check if a set of nodes forms an independent set.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCheck if a set of nodes forms an independent set.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L88138-L88253){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.is_independent_set(nodes)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Is independent set](../assets/graphs/is-independent-set.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The same two-by-three ladder on both sides, with the candidate nodes outlined. Left: A, C, E share no edge, so is_independent_set() returns True. Right: A, C, F, where the edge between C and F (shown in the accent color) joins two members, so is_independent_set() returns False.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nAn independent set (also called a stable set) is a set of vertices in a graph where no two\nvertices are adjacent. This method validates whether the given nodes satisfy this property\nby looking at the neighbors of each node and returning `False` as soon as one of them is\nalso in the set.\n\nIndependent sets show up whenever edges represent conflicts: a set of jobs that can run\nat the same time, facilities that are far enough apart, or survey respondents with no\ndirect ties to one another. Use this method to:\n\n- verify a candidate set built by hand or by an external tool\n- confirm the output of `maximal_independent_set()` or `maximum_independent_set()`\n- check one color class of a coloring (every color class must be independent)\n\nEdge direction is ignored: if the graph has `A -> B`, then `A` and `B` cannot both be in\nthe set. Self-loops are ignored, so a node with a self-loop can still belong to an\nindependent set. The empty set and any single node are always independent.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[nodes]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [list[Union[int, str]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The nodes (IDs or labels) to check. Duplicates are harmless. Every node must\n    exist in the graph, otherwise a `NodeNotFoundError` is raised.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   `True` if the nodes form a valid independent set (no edges between them), `False`\n    otherwise.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [NodeNotFoundError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If any of `nodes=` is not a node in the graph.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nAn independent set contains no adjacent vertices, so validation reduces to scanning\nthe neighbors of each node in the set for another member: a single such edge\nwitnesses invalidity. The cost is proportional to the total degree of the nodes in\nthe set, so at most $O(V + E)$. Empty and singleton sets pass trivially. The dual\nproperty, that the *complement* of an independent set is a *vertex cover*, is what\nties this validation to some of the most well-studied problems in combinatorial\noptimization.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~maximal_independent_set`) \n\n:   Grow an independent set until no node can join.\n\n[](`~maximum_independent_set`) \n\n:   Find a large independent set.\n\n[](`~is_vertex_cover`) \n\n:   Check the complement of an independent set.\n\n[](`~is_valid_coloring`) \n\n:   Check that every color class is independent.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nOn a path, `A` and `C` share no edge, but `C` and `D` do:\n\n::: {#47334437 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\n\n(\n    graph.is_independent_set([\"A\", \"C\"]),\n    graph.is_independent_set([\"A\", \"C\", \"D\"]),\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(True, False)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Checking a time slot\n\n`exams()` joins two of the 14 courses at a made-up college when some student takes both,\nso their exams can't share a time slot. The exams in one slot must form an independent\nset. Calculus, History, Literature and Web Design can all go in the same slot, but adding\nEconomics would give some students two exams at once:\n\n::: {#1e30bae2 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nexams = ec.exams()\n\nslot = [\"Calculus\", \"History\", \"Literature\", \"Web Design\"]\n\n(\n    exams.is_independent_set(slot),\n    exams.is_independent_set(slot + [\"Economics\"]),\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(True, False)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nEach slot of a coloring is an independent set, so it passes too:\n\n::: {#5dfc7b17 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncolors = exams.greedy_color(strategy=\"dsatur\")\nslots = {}\nfor course, color in colors.items():\n    slots.setdefault(color, []).append(course)\n\nall(exams.is_independent_set(courses) for courses in slots.values())\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\nTrue\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#4c6f3936 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nexams.plot(\n    highlight=[\"Calculus\", \"History\", \"Literature\", \"Web Design\"],\n    label_by=\"label\", seed=5,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d